1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:01,580
Business reporters have a

2
00:00:01,580 --> 00:00:03,510
better word than "good."

3
00:00:03,510 --> 00:00:04,470
Buoyant.

4
00:00:04,470 --> 00:00:05,820
BOY-uhnt.

5
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:08,120
Stress on the first syllable.

6
00:00:08,120 --> 00:00:10,250
Buoyant means it floats.

7
00:00:10,250 --> 00:00:11,260
In business,

8
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:14,440
it means rising and optimistic.

9
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:15,290
For example,

10
00:00:15,290 --> 00:00:19,060
"The labour market remains buoyant despite layoffs."

11
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:19,710
At work,

12
00:00:19,710 --> 00:00:21,200
swap "good" for "buoyant":

13
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:24,380
"Sales are buoyant this quarter."

14
00:00:24,380 --> 00:00:26,220
Subscribe to The Fluent Edge

15
00:00:26,220 --> 00:00:28,260
for more words like this.
